        THE BUY-SIDE PSA. This is the shape that exists today: DPEG is the buyer, the paper
        comes from the seller's counsel, and Ball_In_Court__c 'Seller' correctly names the
        counterparty. Parented by Opportunity__c; Disposition__c stays blank.

        ⚠ BOTH RECORD TYPES EXPOSE THE SAME FOUR Negotiation_Status__c VALUES, AND THAT IS THE
        POINT - IT IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT TO BE "FIXED" LATER. Initial Draft -> Revised -> Ready
        for Execution -> Executed are ALREADY exactly the four states the client document names
        for the sell-side PSA, so unlike LOI__c and NDA__c there is no second vocabulary to
        carry. Contract_Review__c therefore needs NO record-type-aware stage map in
        RecordStageAdvanceService - it keeps ONE map serving both types. Anyone adding a
        disposition-only status here should re-read that: it would turn a one-map object into a
        two-map object and drag the Apex change back into scope.

        =====================================================================
        🔴 RETRACTED 2026-08-14 (Phase 3, observation 7). THE PARAGRAPH DIRECTLY ABOVE IS NOW
        FALSE IN EVERY CLAUSE, AND ITS CLOSING WARNING IS AN EXACT DESCRIPTION OF WHAT HAPPENED.
        =====================================================================

        RETRACTED, verbatim: "BOTH RECORD TYPES EXPOSE THE SAME FOUR Negotiation_Status__c
        VALUES... Contract_Review__c therefore needs NO record-type-aware stage map in
        RecordStageAdvanceService - it keeps ONE map serving both types."

        🔴 IT CLOSES WITH: "Anyone adding a disposition-only status here should re-read that: it
        would turn a one-map object into a two-map object and drag the Apex change back into
        scope." THAT IS EXACTLY WHAT THIS CHANGE DOES - from the other direction. No
        disposition-only status was added; an ACQUISITION-only set was. The consequence is
        identical and the Apex change was in scope as requirements C9.

        🔴 THE NEXT SENTENCE IS FALSE AS OF 2026-08-14. IT IS KEPT ONLY AS THE RETRACTED TEXT.
        DO NOT ACT ON IT; THE CORRECTION IS DIRECTLY BELOW. ⚠ THIS IS THE SENTENCE THAT
        GENERATED A PHANTOM OPEN ITEM AT REVIEW - this file is where a reader lands asking "what
        does observation 7 still owe?", and the answer they found was a description of work that
        had already shipped.
        [FALSE] "requirements C9 requires CONTRACT_REVIEW_NEXT_STAGE to be SPLIT, and that
        class's header still asserts the two types point at ONE map shared BY REFERENCE,
        'deliberately', and that 'copying it would invite the two to drift apart'. That prose is
        now wrong and is DEVELOPER work to correct - it is not fixable from this file." [END FALSE]

        ⇒ THE SPLIT IS DELIVERED. There is no shared map in RecordStageAdvanceService:
          - the doc block preceding the acquisition map now OPENS with "🔴 THE SHARED MAP IS
            GONE. THIS IS THE SPLIT ITS OWN COMMENT PREDICTED." (~line 645), and the sentence
            below it names the old CONTRACT_REVIEW_NEXT_STAGE object as HISTORY (~line 646);
          - CONTRACT_REVIEW_ACQUISITION_NEXT_STAGE is declared at ~line 723 and
            CONTRACT_REVIEW_DISPOSITION_NEXT_STAGE at ~line 749 - two separate map objects, not
            one referenced twice;
          - the StageConfig at ~lines 1157 and 1159 points Acquisition_PSA at the first and
